speechtext:
REAFFIRMATION OF SUPPORT FOR INDUSTRY Hon. Doug Lewis (Minister of State and Minister of State (Treasury Board)) moved:
WHEREAS the fur industry plays a vital role in our traditional rural economy;
AND WHEREAS well-managed trapping, as practised in Canada, is in accordance with the principles of the world conservation strategy;
AND WHEREAS Canada is a world leader in humane trap research;
AND WHEREAS this House has previously affirmed its opposition to a proposed resolution before the British Parliament on the labelling of fur products from Canada;
BE IT RESOLVED THAT the House of Commons reaffirm its unanimous support of the Canadian fur industry in recognition of its economic importance to the country and its importance in sustaining resource development economies of both native and Northern communities;
AND THAT the House of Commons reaffirm its opposition to trade distorting measures by foreign governments, such as are now being proposed for consideration by the European Parliament.
